  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(F=re^{i\\theta},\\) then \\(\\frac{1}{F}=r^{-1}e^{-i\\theta}.\\) Because \\(F\\) is outside the unit circle in quadrant I, its reciprocal is inside the unit circle in quadrant IV, with the reflected argument. Only point \\(C\\) has those properties.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "For \\(z=re^{i\\theta},\\) its reciprocal has modulus \\(\\frac{1}{r}\\)",
        "The reciprocal reflects the argument across the real axis and moves inside the unit circle"
      ],
